      "raw_response": "SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract supports the claim that aPKCz (aPKCz) causes tumour enhancement by affecting glutamine metabolism. The abstract states that PKC\u03b6 deficiency in cancer cells allows them to reprogram their metabolism to utilize glutamine through the serine biosynthetic pathway in the absence of glucose. It also mentions that PKC\u03b6 inhibits the expression of two key enzymes of the glutamine pathway, PHGDH and PSAT1, and phosphorylates PHGDH to inhibit its enzymatic activity. These findings directly support the claim that aPKCz affects glutamine metabolism, leading to tumour enhancement. Additionally, the abstract notes that the loss of PKC\u03b6 in mice results in enhanced intestinal tumorigenesis, further supporting the claim.",
